{"book":"equations","bookTitle":"Equations and inequalities","concept":4,"title":"Equations with brackets","grades":"Grade 8","goal":"I can solve equations that have brackets and like terms.","teach":"First make each side simpler: expand the brackets and collect like terms. Then solve as before. 3(x + 2) = 21 → 3x + 6 = 21 → 3x = 15 → x = 5.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:312px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 86\"><text x=\"106.0\" y=\"18.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">x</text><text x=\"201.0\" y=\"18.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"38.0\" y=\"59.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><rect x=\"46.0\" y=\"26.0\" width=\"120.0\" height=\"56.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"106.0\" y=\"59.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">3x</text><rect x=\"166.0\" y=\"26.0\" width=\"70.0\" height=\"56.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"201.0\" y=\"59.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">6</text></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">3(x + 2) = 3x + 6</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Solve 2(x − 3) + 4x = 30.","steps":["Expand: 2x − 6 + 4x = 30.","Collect like terms: 6x − 6 = 30.","6x = 36, so x = 6. Check: 2 × 3 + 24 = 30. <span style=\"font-family:'TeX Gyre Pagella'\">✓</span>"]},"watch":"Multiply every term inside the bracket: 5(x − 2) = 5x − 10, not 5x − 2.","qs":[{"text":"Solve 5(y − 2) = 35.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"y","a":"9","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"5y − 10 = 35","steps":"1. Rule (distributive law): a(b + c) = ab + ac. Expand the brackets first, then solve.<br>2. 5y − 10 = 35<br>3. Add 10: 5y = 45<br>4. y = 9"},{"text":"Solve 3x + 2x − 4 = 21.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"x","a":"5","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"5x − 4 = 21","steps":"1. Rule: collect like terms first.<br>2. 3x + 2x = 5x, so 5x − 4 = 21<br>3. Add 4: 5x = 25<br>4. x = 5"},{"text":"Solve 2(3m + 1) = 26.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"m","a":"4","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"6m + 2 = 26","steps":"1. Rule (distributive law): a(b + c) = ab + ac. Expand the brackets first, then solve.<br>2. 6m + 2 = 26<br>3. Subtract 2: 6m = 24<br>4. m = 4"}]}